  "question": {
    "text": "If in a circular coil $A$ of radius $R$, current I is flowing and in another coil $B$ of radius $2 R$ a current $2 \\mathrm{l}$ is flowing, then the ratio of the magnetic fields $\\mathrm{B}_{\\mathrm{A}}$ and $\\mathrm{B}_{\\mathrm{B}}$, produced by them will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n1/2\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n4",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "In coil A, B $=\\frac{\\mu_0}{4 \\pi} \\frac{2 \\pi \\mathrm{I}}{\\mathrm{R}} . \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{B} \\alpha \\frac{\\mathrm{I}}{\\mathrm{R}}$; Hence, $\\frac{\\mathrm{B}_1}{\\mathrm{~B}_2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_1}{\\mathrm{R}_1} \\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{R}_2}{\\mathrm{I}_2}=\\frac{2}{2}=1$"
  }
}